WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:08.150
The new morning we've finally found

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:08.150
Yatto mitsuketa atarashii asa wa

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:12.190
is being hampered by the past.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:12.190
Tsukihi ga jama wo suru

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:17.660
What we chased after wasn't the future,

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:17.660
Mukau saki wa tsugi ja nakute

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:21.490
but the past so full of remorse.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:21.490
Sugi bakari oikaketa

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:27.960
The ruthless memories won't stop playing;

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:27.960
Nariyamanai yousha nai omoide tachi wa

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.050
they won't be forgiving us for a long time.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.050
Yurushite kuresou nimonai

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.890
It's about now that a teardrop

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.890
Sorosoro kana tesaguri tsukareta hoho wo

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:42.560
beings to roll down my fatigued cheeks.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:42.560
Kattou ga koboreochiru

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:47.810
Will this rain ever stop?

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:47.810
Ame wa itsuka yamunodeshouka

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:53.030
I've been freezing for a long time.

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:53.030
Zuibun nagai aida tsumetai

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:58.320
Why does the rain continue to fix on me?

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:58.320
Ame wa doushite boku wo erabuno

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.080
I wonder if it could embrace me.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.080
Tsutsumarete iikana

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:07.870
Today, the rain falls again;

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:07.870
Ame wa yamu koto wo shirazuni

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:13.090
endlessly it falls knowing no end.

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:13.090
Kyou mo furitsuzukukeredo

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:18.130
We nestle close to each other to share the warmth

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:18.130
Sotto sashidashita kasa no naka de

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:29.850
under this umbrella, you gently held out to me.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:29.850
Nukumori ni yorisoinagara

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.000
Combined Strength

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.000
Combined Strength

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:38.320
A philosopher's stone!

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:39.780
Where did he get that?!

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:45.790
Smoke screening again?

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.710
Like I'll fall for that again!

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:38.840
A flash bang?!

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:42.390
That one was a decoy!

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.890
Nothing less to be expected from the power of a philosopher's stone.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.390
One transmutation after another...!

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:49.430
You...!

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:06.450
The power of a philosopher's stone never ceases to amaze me.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:10.710
I've used it before, so I know.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.080
And that's why I'm confused about something.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:19.760
Why don't you use that power to get your body back?

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:26.300
Since you have the stone, it'll be easy to run from us.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:30.930
Once you get away, you can use the power to get you and your brother's bodies back.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:34.650
And doesn't that conclude your journey?

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:38.230
If we did that, we wouldn't be able to save everyone.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:40.860
It's to fulfill your dearest wish.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:45.950
In order to gain something, one must sacrifice.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:47.990
Hey,

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:51.370
why are you saying there are only two options?

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:58.420
Getting our bodies back, or saving everyone.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:01.630
It's strange to think that only one of those can be granted.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:08.680
Why don't you consider the possibility of getting our bodies back, and at the same time, saving everyone?

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:13.270
What about the law of equivalent exchange?

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:20.650
I think that in order for humanity to progress, we must seek a possibility without being bound by principles.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.150
I see.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:29.580
If that comes true, it'll be recognized by the world as a new principle.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:32.200
Right?

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:38.750
Then you should prepare another possibility.

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:46.130
The possibility of the two of you not getting your bodies back, and not being able to save anyone either.

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:02.280
There's more on the way!

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:18.120
Okay! We can at least pierce his skin!

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:23.340
That hurt...

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.260
I'm gonna die...

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:27.220
This is such a drag...

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:32.010
Dying is such a drag...

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:36.100
Such a drag...

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:41.060
It's going to be such a drag...

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:43.110
...to have to go all out...

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:43.980
What?!

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:47.900
Major General Armstrong!

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:48.860
Put down your weapons!

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:53.120
What the hell is that giant?!

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:09.800
That was...!

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:10.800
Yeah.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.810
I... missed...

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:24.900
W-What speed...!

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:27.110
Sloth the Lazy.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:28.860
Sister!

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:31.200
Just barely grazed.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.200
Did you see that?

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:36.290
Only slightly.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:39.830
Moving at that speed while weighing so much...

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:42.580
It's almost unfair.

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:45.170
Yeah, I'm...

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:48.090
...the fastest Homunculus.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:53.430
Alex!

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:59.310
I think... he's so fast that he can't even control his direction.

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:01.810
Shit-

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:09.320
Finally... I hit.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.460
What a beautiful sound.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:27.130
The clashing of strong wills produces the most beautiful of sounds.

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:34.970
Alphonse Elric is still nearby.

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:36.510
I'm sure of it.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.930
He won't die that easy.

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:47.520
Right there!

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:58.200
That again? How unexciting.

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:00.040
It's futile.

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:13.010
I told you, I can sense where you are by smell.

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:15.640
Checkmate.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:17.680
I wouldn't be so sure.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:20.930
This is where the tenacity of humans comes in!

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:27.060
Even if you have a philosopher's stone,

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:29.150
there's no way you can beat us on your own-

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:30.190
I'm not on my own!

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:34.820
Where did you hide the stone?!

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:40.160
It couldn't be...

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:44.080
The motive behind this cloud of dust is...

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:46.080
...to know the direction of the wind?

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:52.260
He must have something up his sleeve within the leeward where my sense of smell is useless...

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:56.050
Behind me?!

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:05.600
It can't be...!

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:08.600
How can he move with that wound...?!

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:16.240
Doctor Marcoh!

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:31.540
An ice cream truck, right?

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.670
Yeah. Don't miss it.

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:34.340
Right.

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:38.380
Alchemy is so useful, isn't it?

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:41.760
It's a simple matter to change the appearance of a motor vehicle.

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:48.730
We can't go in through here either.

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:52.900
All the gates that allow entry into the Central Headquarters have been sealed off.

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:54.820
What should we do?

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:56.190
Force our way through?

00:09:56.690 --> 00:10:01.780
No, leave the rough jobs up to the Briggs soldiers.

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:04.410
We'll use an underground route.

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:05.200
Roger.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:07.460
We're going to split up now.

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:11.380
I want you all to accompany the madam and head to the location.

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:12.630
Roger.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:31.440
Good thing I'm meaty.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:38.070
Can't underestimate the power of a philosopher's stone, I guess.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:42.950
Their legs!

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:44.240
Aim for their legs!

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:43.800
What?!

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:47.640
Alex!

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:50.930
Just a minor dislocated joint.

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:52.770
What about you, Sister?

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:55.690
Just a broken bone or two.

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:18.840
Sister!

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:30.890
I want to hurry up and kill you...

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:32.310
...so I can nap.

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:46.700
He stopped?!

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:55.120
He's hesitant to stab Kimblee?

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:58.500
But why would someone like him...

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:01.340
I see now.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:05.590
Just as you said, humans are tenacious.

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:09.430
However, you all won't be able to beat us.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:12.770
As long as...

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:16.020
...our father is seated right over there.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:28.200
Well, before that, you all need to find a way to get out of this situation.

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:41.960
Who?!

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:48.180
I did it...

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:51.680
I sure did it!

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:53.680
Yoki?!

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:56.430
Nice one, mustache man!

00:13:57.890 --> 00:14:00.190
I didn't expect you  to show up!

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:02.770
I can't let you guys have all the spotlight!

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:05.570
Let me show off too, geez!

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:07.150
Did you see that?!

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:10.570
I, Yoki, gave the strongest Homunculus a good beatdown!

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:12.950
You saw it!

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:15.370
Where did you get this car?!

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:17.910
It's the one Kimblee rode here in.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:21.790
I'm having the drivers take a little break.

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:24.920
Not bad, Doctor Marcoh.

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:30.760
Step on it!

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:47.740
Shut up and drive!

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:49.280
Drive as fast as you can!

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:52.950
I don't plan on fighting that monster head-on again!

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:55.620
Drive to Central!

00:14:55.620 --> 00:15:00.790
We need to meet up with Ed and the others and defeat Father before that thing catches up with us!

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:14.300
Brave humans sure are easy to trick.

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:27.320
Oh good, you're still alive.

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:35.160
I like the new color of your suit, Kimblee.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:39.160
Now I know why they call lions the "king of beasts".

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:42.330
Obeying the rule of "survival of the fittest",

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:45.790
he gouged out your throat.

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:53.880
I guess humans really are of no importance to this world.

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:09.820
You were saying something about wanting to see what option this world would choose, right?

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:17.740
It would be a disgrace if you were to just die here like this.

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:28.210
But don't worry.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:35.050
You're going to continue to live inside me.

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:57.070
What... happened...?

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:02.330
Alex!

00:17:07.630 --> 00:17:11.920
Since he rushes at you on his own, all you have to do is wait for him.

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:19.600
Can you stand, Sister?

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:27.730
Now that I recall, a shoot-on-sight order has been issued for me.

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:28.940
What?!

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:30.440
That won't do!

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:33.440
I'm going to inherit the Armstrong household,

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:36.360
so I can't have you die until you complete the formalities!

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:38.070
You don't need to worry about that.

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:42.030
I've made it so that the mansion will go to Mustang if I were to die.

00:17:42.030 --> 00:17:44.950
You made a promise like that without even discussing it with your family?!

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:49.500
He's better than a failure like you by a hair.

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:52.960
Is that how you're supposed to treat someone who came to your rescue?!

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:55.970
What's... going on?

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:02.140
Enemy raid?

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:05.140
Don't tell me... it's Mustang's squad?!

00:18:42.340 --> 00:18:43.720
W-What the hell?!

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:46.140
Shooting them doesn't do a thing!

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:48.310
Are they soldiers from Briggs?!

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:49.310
Moron!

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:54.480
Don't confuse my burly men with those scrawny blue monsters!

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:57.570
They're probably the same kind of thing as this is.

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:02.240
The one who commanded you fools is probably behind it.

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:06.040
We were never told of this!

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:11.170
I don't think they care whether or not you were told.

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:19.420
What will you do?

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:23.220
Us siblings can fight those monsters.

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:25.760
But...

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:53.790
So, what will you do?!

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:57.960
Are you going to kill us and end up being eaten by monsters,

00:19:57.960 --> 00:20:01.170
or will you cooperate with us to destroy those fiends?!

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:04.680
Learn to think for yourself!

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:10.180
You!

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:16.900
Again?!

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:31.660
It's no use.

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:35.710
They're soldier dolls that were injected with philosopher's stones.

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:38.130
It'll take more than that to kill them!

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:45.340
See? Look at that.

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:52.470
I got stronger by absorbing them because you keep dodging my attacks.

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:58.310
You don't get it at all.

00:20:58.310 --> 00:21:01.730
It would be troublesome if those dolls were to all rush at me,

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:04.240
but it's simple as pie to run away if it's only you chasing me!

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:06.490
Bullshit!

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:15.500
These dolls have been injected with philosopher's stones.

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:16.960
That's why they won't die.

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:20.040
So the secret to immortality really is in those stones...?

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:23.710
It's to save my clan!

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:25.970
I need to obtain the secret to immortality!

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:35.180
It hurts...

00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:36.690
Pain...

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:39.770
There's still  more of them?!

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:42.190
There's no end to them!

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:49.620
I'm almost out of stings!

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:52.330
I'm just about out of saliva as well.

00:21:59.830 --> 00:22:00.880
Dammit!

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:03.750
Shit!

00:22:05.170 --> 00:22:05.710
Ed!

00:22:15.430 --> 00:22:18.140
It's always so unruly wherever I find you.

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:24.690
Shall I lend you a hand,

00:22:25.730 --> 00:22:26.780
Fullmetal?

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:42.760
Ever since that day passed,

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:42.760
Ano hi kara zutto

00:22:42.760 --> 00:22:47.010
I promised myself that I'd never cry.

00:22:42.760 --> 00:22:47.010
Nakanaito kimetekitakedo

00:22:47.550 --> 00:22:52.560
But even while I hoarded up the pain,

00:22:47.550 --> 00:22:52.560
Itami wo kasanetemo

00:22:52.560 --> 00:22:57.670
there was something I couldn't forgive myself for.

00:22:52.560 --> 00:22:57.670
Nanika wo yurusezu ni ita

00:22:59.150 --> 00:23:01.110
I'll never be able

00:22:59.150 --> 00:23:01.110
Mou modorenai

00:23:01.110 --> 00:23:03.610
to return to those days.

00:23:01.110 --> 00:23:03.610
Ikutsumo no hibi

00:23:03.610 --> 00:23:08.700
I'm still powerless.

00:23:03.610 --> 00:23:08.700
Boku wa mada nanimo dekizuni

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:13.950
I watch as the shards of memories disappear, one by one;

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:13.950
Kimi no ita kioku no kakera

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:19.820
memories of when you were still with me.

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:19.820
Mata hitotsu kieteyuku

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:22.840
I long to become

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:22.840
Kyou yori motto

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:25.590
stronger than I am now,

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:25.590
Tsuyoku naritai

00:23:25.590 --> 00:23:30.730
so that my voice will eventually reach you.

00:23:25.590 --> 00:23:30.730
Kono koe ga itsuka todokuyouni

00:23:30.730 --> 00:23:33.100
If the wind happens to stop

00:23:30.730 --> 00:23:33.100
Arukitsuzukete

00:23:33.100 --> 00:23:35.810
in the midst of my long journey,

00:23:33.100 --> 00:23:35.810
Kaze ga yandara

00:23:35.810 --> 00:23:40.520
I'll look up at the sky in search of you.

00:23:35.810 --> 00:23:40.520
Kimi wo sagashite sora miageruyo

00:23:41.270 --> 00:23:47.860
Beyond the daybreak, a ray of light breaks free.

00:23:41.270 --> 00:23:47.860
Yoake no saki ni hikari ga sasuyo

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:53.410
A rainbow spans across the sky.

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:53.410
Niji ga kakaruyo

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:03.210
When people arrive at the truth,

00:24:03.210 --> 00:24:07.340
they lay their hearts bare.

00:24:07.340 --> 00:24:13.380
They are unable to stop themselves, nor do they have the luxury of choice.

00:24:14.550 --> 00:24:18.760
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

00:24:18.760 --> 00:24:22.780
Episode 53, Flame of Vengeance.

00:24:18.780 --> 00:24:22.780
Flame of Vengeance

00:24:23.350 --> 00:24:26.900
Reduce everything to ashes.
